description:
Regional Workshop on Strengthening National Capacities for Climate Change and Health Vulnerability and Adaptation Assessments (H-VAAs) and Health National Adaptation Plans (H-NAPs) in the Eastern Mediterranean Region, organised by the Climate Change, Health and Environment Unit (CHE) of the WHO Regional Office for the Eastern Mediterranean

The main objectives are to:
•	Apply a three-layer analytical model as the regional standard for national H-VAAs;
•	Integrate WASH, One Health, and migration/displacement into the assessment process;
•	Develop structured H-VAA workplans or H-NAP transition strategies through hands-on country group work;
•	Identify pathways for climate finance and strengthen health positioning for COP31; and
•	Establish academic partnerships for ongoing technical support.

keyOutputs:
-Key messages and cross-cutting priorities for a minimum gender-responsive protection checklist for PHC workers; 
- session minutes and presentations; 
- follow-up entry points including stakeholder consultations, an opinion piece and possible collaboration with partners on workforce protection in emergencies and high-risk settings.
